  "code_facts": [
    "DATA_VALID is PCS status_vector(1), synchronized into independent SYS clock. It represents link synchronization, not completed auto-negotiation or successful IP communication.",
    "Normal PRBS selection000 makes DONT_RESET_ON_DATA_ERROR0 through OR-of-PRBS select. Automatic retry is not simply disabled.",
    "MONITOR_DATA_VALID retries only after100us timeout while invalid; transitions back toFSM_DONE on validity reset the timeout.",
    "Native debug trace records every masked state change until256 events; DATA_VALID bit23 alone is excluded from trigger mask. Hence intervals here are FSM-state intervals, not an exhaustive raw-data-valid waveform."
  ],
  "inference": "Captured bad-state FSM repeatedly returns toDONE before the100us invalid-data retry threshold. This supports a recovery blind spot for intermittent synchronization rather than a stopped FSM. It is compatible with prior bad recovered-clock ratio/8b10b errors and PMA recovery.",
